{"name":"Kingfisher","hex":"#3a5760","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kingfisher","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city, the county seat of Kingfisher County, Oklahoma, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kingfisher"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kingfisher","blocks":[{"text":"Kingfishers are a family, the Alcedinidae, of small to medium-sized, brightly coloured birds in the order Coraciiformes. They have a cosmopolitan distribution: most species live in the tropical regions of Africa, Asia, and Oceania, but they can also be found in Europe and the Americas. They can be found in deep forests near calm ponds and small rivers. The family contains 118 species and is divided into three subfamilies and 19 genera. All kingfishers have large heads, long, sharp, pointed bills, short legs, and stubby tails. Most species have bright plumage with only small differences between the sexes. Most species are tropical in distribution, and a slight majority are found only in forests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten.jpg/330px-Alcedo_azurea_-_Julatten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingfisher","wikidata":"Q8154335"},{"title":"Kingfisher (beer)","blocks":[{"text":"Kingfisher is an Indian beer brewed by United Breweries Group, Bangalore, India. The brand was first introduced in 1857 and then relaunched in 1978 by Vijay Mallya. With a market share of over 36% in India, it is also available in 52 other countries as of 2013."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Kingfisher_beer_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingfisher_(beer)","wikidata":"Q1572281"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kingfisher_range.png/500px-Kingfisher_range.pn